#![allow(unused-imports)]
$!"inner, not useful now"

/* todo
- $"no-derive-debug"
    - in u->rs, if there's no $"no-derive-debug",
        add #[derive(Debug)] in rs

        that is to say, the next time you open the .u file, the struct which had no #[derive(Debug)]
        will have #[derive(Debug)] now.
        so the benefit is less thinking about Debug and typing, since most places need Debug anyway
    - in rs->u, if there's no Debug in #[derive()] in rs,
        add $"no-derive-debug" in u
- $"no-s"
    in u->rs, if there's no $"no-s",
        add "let s = self;"
    in rs->u, if there's no "let s = self;" as the first item in method body,
        add $"no-s"
    else
        delete the first item

- open *.rs: read *.rs -> rust's ast -> write .*.u
- close .*.u: rustfmt --edition 2024 *.rs

- place comments in the right order in u-to-rust
- when writing to .*.u, align multi-line struct members and other stuff with least gap of 3 spaces
*/

